ghtGBM + XGBoost + CatBoost with class balancing\n7. **Meta-Stacking** &#8212; LR meta-learner on OOF predictions + polynomial interactions\n\n### Generalization verification (4 checks):\n| Check | What it measures | Pass criteria |\n|---|---|---|\n| Fold Score Stability | Consistency across CV folds | Std &lt; 0.005 |\n| Prediction Distribution | OOF vs test alignment | Mean drift &lt; 0.02 |\n| Adversarial Validation | Train/test distinguishability | AUC &lt; 0.55 |\n| Learning Curves | Train-val gap trend | Gap &lt; 0.03 |\n\n### Anti-overfitting measures:\n- &#9989; 5-fold Stratified CV with stable fold scores\n- &#9989; Early stopping (150 rounds patience)\n- &#9989; Class-balanced training (is_unbalance / scale_pos_weight / auto_class_weights)\n- &#9989; Original data down-weighted to prevent distribution shift\n- &#9989; OOF target encoding prevents train leakage\n- &#9989; Low-variance meta-learner (LogisticRegression) on high-variance base models\n\n</div>\n\n<br>\n<div style=\"text-align:center;color:#22d3ee;font-size:1.1em;padding:15px;\">If this notebook helped you, an <b>upvote</b> would mean the world! &#128588;</div>","metadata":{}}]}